<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  What the hardened runtime is asked to allow, and nothing more.

  Notarization requires the hardened runtime, which switches off several things
  by default; each entitlement here switches one back on for a stated reason. A
  shorter list is a better one, so nothing is added speculatively — if a launch
  fails under the hardened runtime, the crash names the protection it hit and
  that is what earns an entry.

  Not sandboxed: this is a Developer ID app distributed outside the App Store,
  which runs a local gateway and spawns an agent process. The App Sandbox would
  need entitlements for both and buys nothing for this distribution channel.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!--
    The webview's JavaScript engine compiles to native code at runtime, which
    the hardened runtime forbids without this. Every Tauri app on macOS needs
    it; without it the panel is a blank window.
  -->
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
